From 6787b2a6b873166e58bccb9c6a20a8d59defdf85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:18:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 18/26] ling: speed levers behind switches, default off:
 TF_LING_ROCE=1 (main's RoCE one-shot gathers beside NCCL, both ranks),
 TF_LING_GRAPHS=1 (one sequence's verify windows and chained MTP drafts as
 CUDA graphs on main's graph cache, keyed by rows, KDA copy and an 8-chunk MLA
 bucket; trailing chunks merge as nothing), TF_LING_MTP_DRAFTS (the chain's
 most drafts, 1..5, default 3), TF_LING_PROMPT_TILES=1 (EXL3 prompt
 projections on main's tensor-core tiles); ling-tp --window/--time/--mtp
 (every row's logits and drafts hashed; per-width verify and draft timing)

